# A1/A1.1/A1_08_places_and_directions.letz
# Source: Quizlet "A1 Basics Beginner Luxembourgish Lesson 8"
#   https://quizlet.com/_h2svv7
# Comma-separated noun forms split; gender markers stripped;
# (no) and (ewech) optional words produce extra @lu variants;
# (to) optional EN endings produce extra @en variants.

@lesson A1.08 "Places & Directions"

# --- Place nouns (Quizlet cards 1-12) ---
@word d'Haus = house
@word Haiser = houses

@word d'Gebai = building
@word Gebaier = buildings

@word de Buttek = shop
@word Butteker = shops

@word d'Gemeng = commune
@word Gemengen = communes

@word den Theater = theatre
@word Theateren = theatres

@word d'Kierch = church
@word Kierchen = churches

@word d'Schoul = school
@word Schoulen = schools

@word d'Bréck = bridge
@word Brécken = bridges

@word de Kino = cinema
@word Kinoen = cinemas

@word d'Klinick = hospital
@word Klinicken = hospitals

@word d'Apdikt = pharmacy
@word Apdikten = pharmacies

@word de Café = café
@word Caféen = cafés

# --- Directional phrases (Quizlet cards 35-40) ---
@word laanscht de Kleederrayon = past the clothing aisle
@word de Rez-de-chaussée = the ground floor
@word den éischte Stack = the first floor
@word Richtung Mamer = in the direction of Mamer
@word op der rietser Säit = on the right hand side
@word op der lénker Säit = on the left hand side

# --- Vocabulary from sentences (coverage backfill) ---
@word de Park = park
@word d'Stad = city
@word d'Wollek = cloud
@word lénks = left
@word riets = right
@word riichtaus = straight ahead
@word wäit = far
@word hannert = behind
@word niewent = next to
@word tëschent = between

# --- Sentences (Quizlet cards 13-34) ---

@sentence
@lu De Restaurant ass niewent der Kierch.
@en The restaurant is next to the church.
@distractor-en school
@distractor-en bridge
@distractor-en behind
@distractor-lu Schoul
@distractor-lu Bréck
@distractor-lu hannert

@sentence
@lu D'Emma ass an der Schoul.
@en Emma is in school.
@distractor-en church
@distractor-en home
@distractor-lu Kierch
@distractor-lu doheem

@sentence
@lu De Rick steet tëschent zwee Beem.
@en Rick is standing between two trees.
@distractor-en hospital
@distractor-en pharmacy
@distractor-en behind
@distractor-lu Klinick
@distractor-lu Apdikt
@distractor-lu hannert

@sentence
@lu De Park ass no bei der Bank.
@lu De Park ass bei der Bank.
@en The park is close to the bank.
@distractor-en café
@distractor-en shop
@distractor-lu Café
@distractor-lu Buttek

@sentence
@lu D'Post ass wäit ewech vun der Bank.
@lu D'Post ass wäit vun der Bank.
@en The post office is far away from the bank.
@distractor-en building
@distractor-en commune
@distractor-lu Gebai
@distractor-lu Gemeng

@sentence
@lu De Café ass vis-à-vis vun der Apdikt.
@en The café is opposite the pharmacy.
@distractor-en theatre
@distractor-en church
@distractor-lu Theater
@distractor-lu Kierch

@sentence
@lu De Vic steet hannert der Bréck.
@en Vic is standing behind the bridge.
@distractor-en school
@distractor-en cinema
@distractor-en in front of
@distractor-lu Schoul
@distractor-lu Kino
@distractor-lu virun

@sentence
@lu D'Martine steet virun der Gemeng.
@en Martine is standing in front of the commune.
@distractor-en bridge
@distractor-en hospital
@distractor-en behind
@distractor-lu Bréck
@distractor-lu Klinick
@distractor-lu hannert

@sentence
@lu Ech sinn op der Post.
@en I'm at the post office.
@distractor-en theatre
@distractor-en church
@distractor-lu Theater
@distractor-lu Kierch

@sentence
@lu Ech sinn an de Wolleken.
@en My head is in the clouds.
@distractor-en city
@distractor-en building
@distractor-lu Stad
@distractor-lu Gebai

@sentence
@lu Ech ginn an den Theater.
@en I'm going to the theatre.
@distractor-en cinema
